From b0183a62150e0d91c4bb924d6ec524c5e74ebb8d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rudi Heitbaum <rudi@heitbaum.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 21:30:00 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 005/213] LOCAL: drm/rockchip: vop: disable AFBC on RK3399

Kodi is unusable on RK3399 because the vop advertises AFBC on win0.

Two independent failures follow from it. The AFBC decoder is programmed
with hreg_block_split hardcoded to 0, and without SPLIT mode it cannot
sustain a 3840 wide scanout, so a 4K desktop is displayed as a black
screen. Nothing rejects it: vop_plane_atomic_check() validates the AFBC
format, the source offset and the rotation, but not the width, so the
atomic commit succeeds and the picture is simply lost.

Separately, win0 is the only plane that can scan out AFBC and its zpos
is fixed at 0. A compositor that needs a gui layer above a video layer
therefore has to place the gui on win1, which is linear only, so no
valid plane pair exists and hardware video playback cannot be set up at
all. On Kodi this ends in "Cannot find a Video Plane .. together with a
Gui Plane ..", a fallback to a GLES path that does not accept drm_prime,
and no video.

Both disappear when the gui buffer is linear. Stop advertising the
modifier until SPLIT mode is implemented and the plane pairing has a
solution.

Signed-off-by: Rudi Heitbaum <rudi@heitbaum.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_vop_reg.c | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_vop_reg.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_vop_reg.c
index 72301e0a3e0a..828f932f9b6b 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_vop_reg.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_vop_reg.c
@@ -78,7 +78,6 @@ static const uint64_t format_modifiers_win_full[] = {
 };
 
 static const uint64_t format_modifiers_win_full_afbc[] = {
-	ROCKCHIP_AFBC_MOD,
 	DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR,
 	DRM_FORMAT_MOD_INVALID,
 };
